# localnet-setup
localnet-setup

# build
build

# Secrets and machine-local configuration. These are not tracked today, which is
# exactly why they belong here: `docker build` sends the whole working tree, so an
# operator's local .env or an exported validator key would be baked into a layer of
# the published image before anyone noticed. Keeping the list ahead of the accident
# is cheaper than a credential rotation.
.env
.env.*
*.env
.release-env
secret.yml
secrets.yml
*.pem
*.key

# Local agent/audit workspace: holds operator notes with hostnames and addresses.
.workbuddy

# NOTE: `.git` is deliberately NOT ignored. Makefile:4 and :45 stamp
# version.Commit from `git log -1`, which reaches the binary via ldflags; with the
# git directory outside the build context the stamp silently resolves to empty and
# the published image reports no commit at all.
